## Additional Terms and Security Notice

### 1. Security and Privacy
This software implements industry-standard security practices including:
- JWT-based authentication with secure token management
- Password hashing using bcryptjs
- Input validation and sanitization
- CORS protection
- Rate limiting on authentication endpoints

However, users are responsible for:
- Properly configuring environment variables
- Using strong, unique passwords
- Securing their MongoDB instances
- Implementing HTTPS in production
- Regular security updates and monitoring

### 2. Data Protection
When deploying this application, you are responsible for:
- Complying with applicable data protection laws (GDPR, CCPA, etc.)
- Implementing appropriate data backup and recovery procedures
- Securing user data and maintaining privacy
- Obtaining necessary consents for data collection
- Providing users with data access and deletion capabilities

### 3. Third-Party Services
This application may integrate with third-party services:
- Email providers (for verification and password reset)
- Database hosting services (MongoDB Atlas)
- Authentication providers
- Analytics services (if implemented)

Users must comply with the terms of service and privacy policies of these providers.

